ldn't have. If you have\n     * code that calls @ref wgpuDevicePoll with @c wait=true on WebGL, you\n     * may need to enable this option for \"wait\" to behave how you expect.\n     *\n     * When this is set, @c wgpuQueueOnCompletedWorkDone callbacks will fire\n     * the next time the device is polled, not when work is actually done on\n     * the GPU.\n     */"} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Undefined", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Undefined", :value 0, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment nil} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromHwnd", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromHwnd", :value 1, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment "/**\n     * Use a DXGI swapchain created directly from the window's HWND.\n     *\n     * This does not support transparency but has better support from\n     * developer tooling such as RenderDoc.\n     */"} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromVisual", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromVisual", :value 2, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment "/**\n     * Use a DXGI swapchain created from a DirectComposition visual made\n     * automatically from the window's HWND.\n     *\n     * This creates a single @c IDCompositionVisual over the entire window.\n     * Supports transparency. If you want to manage the composition tree\n     * yourself, create your own device and composition and pass the relevant\n     * visual via the surface target.\n     */"} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Force32", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Force32", :value 2147483647, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment "/**\n     * Use a DXGI swapchain created from a DirectComposition visual made\n     * automatically from the window's HWND.\n     *\n     * This creates a single @c IDCompositionVisual over the entire window.\n     * Supports transparency. If you want to manage the composition tree\n     * yourself, create your own device and composition and pass the relevant\n     * visual via the surface target.\n     */"} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Undefined", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Undefined", :value 0, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment nil} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromHwnd", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromHwnd", :value 1, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment "/**\n     * Use a DXGI swapchain created directly from the window's HWND.\n     *\n     * This does not support transparency but has better support from\n     * developer tooling such as RenderDoc.\n     */"} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromVisual", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_DxgiFromVisual", :value 2, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment "/**\n     * Use a DXGI swapchain created from a DirectComposition visual made\n     * automatically from the window's HWND.\n     *\n     * This creates a single @c IDCompositionVisual over the entire window.\n     * Supports transparency. If you want to manage the composition tree\n     * yourself, create your own device and composition and pass the relevant\n     * visual via the surface target.\n     */"} {:kind "CXCursor_EnumConstantDecl", :spelling "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Force32", :type "CXType_Int", :name "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind_Force32", :value 2147483647, :enum "WGPUDx12SwapchainKind", :raw-comment "/**\n     * Use a DXGI swapchain created from a DirectComposition visual made\n     * automatically from the window's HWND.\n     *\n     * This creates a single @c IDCompositionVisual over the entire window.\n     * Supports transparency. If you want to manage the composition tree\n     * yourself, create your own device and composition and pass t